; ABNF mirror (descriptive, not test-parsed — the real byte-level walker is
; ../📡️.protocol.semio, walked by dsl::walk_protocol) for stdio.semio.audio snapshot
; (binary) — the shared `.semio` binary envelope (store::semio_format::wrap_binary) wrapping the
; REAL varint-length-prefixed SemioAudioSnapshot binary pack (NOT serde_json::to_vec).
document        = envelope-magic token-len token format schema-len schema-bytes sample-rate audio-format payload
envelope-magic  = %x89 %x53 %x45 %x4D %x0D %x0A %x1A %x0A   ; 8 bytes: 0x89 "SEM" CR LF SUB LF
token-len       = 4OCTET                                     ; u32, little-endian
token           = 25OCTET                                    ; UTF-8 "stdio.semio.audio.pack v1"
format          = OCTET                                      ; PACK_BINARY_FORMAT, currently 1
schema-len      = 1*OCTET                                    ; LEB128 varint
schema-bytes    = *OCTET                                     ; UTF-8 schema id, e.g. stdio.semio.audio
sample-rate     = 4OCTET                                     ; u32, little-endian
audio-format    = OCTET                                      ; 0=Pcm8 1=Pcm16 2=Pcm24 3=Pcm32 4=Float32 5=Float64
payload         = *OCTET                                     ; channels/tags — see ../../🦀️.rs's encode_audio_snapshot_binary; opaque here (protocol-array-of-records gap)
